    "body": "pulse task #2907 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:cc87e96684a4c636e584bd247618bede -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2907: Sampler MVP: qualify and deliver one optimized musical-use build\n\nOperation: cc87e96684a4c636e584bd247618bede\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nTarget: one coherent optimized macOS candidate proves the complete reduced MVP and is supplied for actual music making. Acceptance: combine canonicalPR395 source and bounded prerequisites without losing modern Main/UI/selection behavior; demonstrate startup\u2192load/replace\u2192MIDI+Arrange/Console playback\u2192basic controls\u2192Undo/Redo\u2192save/reopen preserving media+tuning. Run repository-required exact-candidate local checks/review on frozen source, including ownership/callback/resource failures and relevant fixture corrections; no hosted CI, waived tests or component pass substitution. Build optimized cargo release using repository delivery tools, provide exact source/build/included issue/PR revisions and a finite user checklist. Packaging, installed provenance, quit/relaunch requirement and manual acceptance are separate truthful facts; preserve running app/projects/media, no force-quit.\n\nOwner: existing sole merger/integration with coordinated existing local native delivery lane when available; no extra chat/worker. Depends on completed load/play/panel/history/persistence and real resource admission. Assemble finite checklist/provenance now; full checks only once coherent frozen source is ready. Completion requires actual requested artifact/delivery evidence, not issue merge or a plan.\n\nSplit from #2789/canonical PR395, goal5 Playable Sampler MVP. Existing implementation/source/history stays intact. Intake draft is planning linkage only until deliberate focused source handoff; no automatic task start, duplicate implementation or replacing existing canonicalPR3